// Every Minecraft 1.0.0 block, by original numeric ID (see docs/blocks-and-items.md).
//
// Fields (only id, name and hardness are required):
//   hardness  1.0.0 mining hardness; negative = unbreakable
//   shape     model, default Cube (see Shape in src/world/block.rs)
//   layer     Opaque (default), Cutout or Translucent
//   solid     entities collide with it (default true)
//   light     light emitted, 0-15 (default 0)
//   cull_same hide faces between two of this block (glass, water)
//   textures  names in assets/textures/blocks/ (without .png), per face. The
//             most specific field wins: north/south/east/west, then
//             top/bottom, then end (top + bottom) or side (four sides), then
//             all. A block with a "front" puts it on south; with placement
//             Facing it's turned toward the player. Leave out for blocks that
//             draw nothing.
//   tint      None (default), GrassTop, Grass, Foliage or Fixed(0xRRGGBB)
//   variants  per-data-value overrides: {data: (name, textures, tint)}
//   tool      tool that mines it fast: Pickaxe, Shovel or Axe
//   harvest   tool needed to drop anything: (tools: [...], tier: Wood)
//   placement Plain (default), Torch (attaches to the clicked face),
//             Facing (front toward the player, data 2-5), Bed (two
//             halves, data 0-3 the direction and 8 the head), Door (two
//             halves, data 0-3 the direction, 4 open and 8 the upper) or
//             Slab(double: id) (joins the same slab below into `double`)
//   activate  what right-clicking it does: Crafting (opens a 3×3 grid),
//             Chest or Furnace (opens its slots), Bed (sleeps) or Door
//             (opens and closes; iron doors have none, needing redstone)
//   fluid     Water or Lava for liquids (swimming, fog, slower mining)
//   burns     (encourage, catch): how readily fire spreads beside it and
//             how readily it burns away (modern FireBlock values)
//   drops     Itself (default; keeps the data value if it has variants),
//             Nothing, All([...]) every drop that rolls, or OneOf([...]) the
//             first that rolls. A drop is (item, data, keep_data, min, max,
//             chance, min_data, max_data, tool, not_tool).
//
// Data values that only encode orientation, growth or fluid level (furnace
// facing, snow height, cake bites...) don't need variants.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
[
    (id: 0, name: "air", hardness: 0.0, drops: Nothing, replaceable: true, shape: None, solid: false),
